  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The half hexagon solves the perimeter problem in a hexagon blanket — without it, the blanket edge is a zigzag of points that cannot lie flat against a border or edge trim. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "flat-construction"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Flat construction"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " in rows (back and forth rather than in the round) gives the straight bottom edge. The same "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "treble-cluster"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "treble cluster"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " structure as the full hexagon is used throughout, with the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "foundation-chain"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "foundation chain"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " setting the base width. Three rows build upward from the base. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "blocking"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Blocking"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " the half hexagon flat is required for accurate tiling."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "type": "materials"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Yarn: DK cotton, approx 15 m per half hexagon. Hook: 4 mm. Notions: tapestry needle, scissors, blocking mat and pins."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "11 cm wide × 6 cm tall in DK cotton on a 4 mm hook. The width must match the full hexagon width (11 cm) for the pieces to tile together."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Chain (ch)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Treble (tr)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "3-treble cluster (3tr cl)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Slip stitch (sl st)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The half hexagon is worked in rows, turning after each row. Ch 5 at the start of each row counts as tr + ch-2 corner. No magic ring is used."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Foundation / Row 1"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 10. Into 6th ch from hook: 3tr cl (first corner). Ch 2. Into same ch: 3tr cl (second corner — ch-2 between gives centre corner sp). Ch 2. Skip 3 ch. Into next ch: 3tr cl. Ch 2. Into same ch: 3tr cl. Turn. (2 corner groups of 2 clusters separated by ch-2, 1 straight edge) = (12 tr total)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 2"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 5 (counts as tr + ch-2). 3tr cl in first ch-2 sp at near end. Ch 1. (3tr cl, ch 2, 3tr cl) in centre ch-2 sp (corner). Ch 1. 3tr cl in next ch-2 sp. Ch 2. 3tr cl in last ch-2 sp. Turn. (6 clusters, 2 ch-2 end sps, 1 ch-2 centre corner, 2 ch-1 side sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 3"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 5 (counts as tr + ch-2). 3tr cl in first ch-2 sp. Ch 1. 3tr cl in ch-1 sp. Ch 1. (3tr cl, ch 2, 3tr cl) in centre corner ch-2 sp. Ch 1. 3tr cl in next ch-1 sp. Ch 1. 3tr cl in next ch-2 sp. Ch 2. 3tr cl in last ch-2 sp. Fasten off. (9 clusters, 2 ch-2 end sps, 1 ch-2 centre corner, 4 ch-1 side sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chart"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "craftChart",
        "attrs": {
          "roundCount": 3
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in ends at both side edges. Wet-block to 11 cm × 6 cm, pinning the straight base chain along the bottom and placing pins at the two outer top corners. The centre top should form a slight V from the corner ch-2 sp."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Joining"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The straight base of the half hexagon joins to the straight edge of a full hexagon blanket. Work the join with slip stitches through corresponding chain-1 side spaces and the top cluster. The angled sides join to the angled sides of the adjacent full hexagons."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine wash at 30 degrees on a gentle cycle. Reshape while damp and dry flat. Re-block if the half hexagon distorts after washing — it needs to remain flat to sit correctly in the blanket."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A quarter hexagon (triangle) fills the blanket corners. Work only rows 1 and 2 of the half hexagon and cut the pattern before the centre corner ch-2 sp — the resulting piece fills one side of the corner. Or extend the half hexagon to 4 rows for a wider perimeter fill if the full hexagon is larger than 11 cm."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}